## Why This Is Asked

This realistic scenario evaluates the ability to design real-time, multi-tenant telemetry systems with proper isolation, versioned ML models, and comprehensive cost controls. The question probes deep understanding of data schema evolution, idempotence, backpressure handling, and governance across AWS DVA primitives.

## Key Concepts

- **Multi-tenant isolation** through partition keys and IAM policies
- **Real-time inference** with Fargate container orchestration
- **Model versioning** and drift detection strategies
- **Data schema design** with backward compatibility
- **Idempotence** for exactly-once processing guarantees
- **Backpressure and retry** handling in streaming systems
- **Cost controls** through quotas and auto-scaling policies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Event schema with tenant isolation
class AnomalyEvent {
  constructor(tenantId, eventId, timestamp, features) {
    this.tenantId = tenantId;
    this.eventId = eventId; // UUID for idempotence
    this.timestamp = timestamp;
    this.features = features;
    this.partitionKey = `${tenantId}:${eventId.slice(-8)}`;
  }
}

// Fargate inference service with model versioning
class InferenceService {
  async processEvent(event) {
    const model = await this.getModelVersion(event.tenantId);
    const score = await model.predict(event.features);

    // Idempotent write to DynamoDB
    await this.writeResult(event, score);

    // Alert routing if threshold exceeded
    if (score > this.getThreshold(event.tenantId)) {
      await this.routeAlert(event, score);
    }
  }
}
```

